  "worked_solution": "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,\u27f9\\,{{(LU)}_{\u23df}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{\u23df}}_{y}=b\\,\u27f9\\,{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=2 \\\\ -4{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=2$ and ${y}_{2}=6.$ \n\nTherefore, $y=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].$",
